# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# METALOID — frontend environment (Vite)
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. Everything here is BUNDLED INTO THE
# BROWSER, so only public values belong in this file.
#
#   SAFE HERE   → VITE_* values, the Supabase URL and the *anon* key
#   NEVER HERE  → service-role key, JWT secret, encryption keys, provider
#                 API keys. Those go in `server/.env` (see server/.env.example)
#                 and stay on the gateway.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Where the MetaIoid gateway lives.
#   Local development: leave unset — the dev server proxies /api to 127.0.0.1:8787
#   Production:        https://<your-gateway-host>
VITE_API_URL=

# ── Supabase (client-safe) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Project Settings → API. The anon key is designed to be public: it grants
# nothing on its own, because every table is protected by Row Level Security
# and every gateway route requires a verified user JWT.
#
# Leave both empty to run METALOID in its local/sandbox mode: no accounts,
# no sync, everything on-device. That mode stays fully supported.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# ⚠️ Never put these in a VITE_ variable (they would ship to the browser):
#    SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY · SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET · METALOID_ENCRYPTION_KEYS
